{
  "about": "Example events for the draft 'Agents in chats' specification (kinds 1201, 1202, and kind 1009 versions of an item). Each example gives the inner Marmot app event's kind, tags and content; its id, pubkey and created_at follow the ordinary app-event envelope. Every id and key below is a synthetic 64-hex placeholder (a repeated two-character pattern), never a real key or event. `readable` says whether a reader following the feature document accepts the event as an agent item (1201, 1009) or request (1202); for kinds 9 and 1111 it is always true. `assumed_id` names the placeholder taken as an example's own event id where other examples refer to it (an edit's `e`, a request's `e`, `settles`, a thread's `E` and `e`); real ids are the hash of the event.",
